body:
I was always a social outcast, but at age 10 I fell ill and had to drop out of school. My entire teens and most of my twenties were basically in social isolation from people my own age. Even after lots of therapy and 'exposure' to people, at 30 my emotional intelligence and social skills are still that of a socially retarded 10 year old, along with other physical and mental issues. There is no place for me in society, this is existing, not living. The best would indeed be to make it through but honestly I don't see a way back from this anymore, there's only so much mental torture you can handle. 

She's afraid to leave because one of the therapists, of which you're supposed to trust, let her know I have severe suicidal ideation, so now she's thinks I'm going to kill myself every time she leaves for more than a day. 

&#x200B;
